                <pb facs="0777" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v02/pg757"/>

                <head>324. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On December 3, 1962, Roger Hilsman
                    transmitted to Secretary of State Rusk
                    research memorandum RFE-59, “The Situation and Short-term Prospects in South
                    Vietnam,” which appraised the internal political situation in South Vietnam over
                    the past year. Although the leaders of South Vietnam apparently believed that
                    the tide was turning against insurgency and subversion, the memorandum concluded
                    that this optimism was premature, and that at best the rate of deterioration had
                    decelerated as United States assistance had increased. For text of RFE-59, see
                        <hi rendition="#italic">United States-Vietnam Relations, 1945-1967</hi>,
                    Book 12, Part I, pages 487-521.</p>
            </div>
